diff --git a/docs/business-rules.md b/docs/business-rules.md
index 7a3126a..d1ffc59 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -65,6 +65,16 @@ ## User Administration
 | Remove user | Admin, owner | Cannot remove the owner; employees lose immediate access to the entity. |
 | Assign role | Admin, owner | Users are **separated by role**; employees receive granular permissions, not admin/owner role. |
 
+## Authentication (staff sessions)
+
+Staff sign in with e-mail and password through a server-side session (no API tokens yet). Implemented in `app/Livewire/Auth/`, `app/Http/Controllers/` and `routes/web.php`.
+
+- **Register:** name, unique e-mail and a password under the app-wide default rule (min. 8 characters, letters, mixed case, numbers). The account starts unverified; the app sends the verification e-mail and the user lands on `home`, which requires a verified e-mail.
+- **Login:** e-mail + password, optional "remember me". Failed attempts are limited to 5 per e-mail and IP; the error is the same whether or not the e-mail exists. A logged-in user cannot switch accounts from the login form.
+- **Password reset:** the forgot-password answer is always the same, so it never reveals which e-mails have an account. Forms are throttled to 6 requests per minute. A reset rotates `remember_token` and does not log the user in.
+- **E-mail verification:** a signed link verifies only the logged-in user whose id and hash it carries; anyone else gets 403. Resending is throttled and sends nothing for an already verified user.
+- **Logout:** POST only; it invalidates the session and regenerates the CSRF token.
+
